File `utils.ts` found. Relevant function code:

```typescript
function filterByKey<K extends string>(obj: Record<K, any>, key: K): Record<K, any> {
  return Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(obj).filter(([k]) => k === key));
}
```

The issue is that `Object.entries` returns an array of `[string, any]` pairs, but your `K` type is constrained to `string`. This causes a type mismatch. To fix this, explicitly cast `k` to `K`:

```typescript
function filterByKey<K extends string>(obj: Record<K, any>, key: K): Record<K, any> {
  return Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(obj).filter(([k]) => k as K === key));
}
```
This should resolve the error.

